{"requests": [
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "ok so our ADK agent is deployed on Cloud Run and the React frontend just POSTs to /run and waits like 20s for the whole answer, which looks terrible. how do I switch to /run_sse and render the text as it streams in? also when the agent calls our lookup_inventory tool I want a little 'Checking inventory…' chip to show up instead of dead air. bonus points if a stream that dies halfway doesn't wipe the partial message, right now it just shows a blank bubble"},
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "Need advice before sprint planning Thursday. We have a Python ADK agent with a human-in-the-loop step (refund approvals over $500) and users want a sidebar listing past conversations they can reopen and keep going. Should we keep building our own fetch/JSON layer in vanilla TS, or adopt something like CopilotKit / assistant-ui / AG-UI on the frontend? Mainly care about how approve/reject prompts and session resume would work in each."},
 {"kind": "elsewhere", "text": "our agent's replies are streaming fine in the browser but the agent keeps forgetting what the user said three turns ago once the session gets long. using VertexAiSessionService. is this a frontend thing? how do I fix it", "needs_instead": "Backend session state and context management in ADK (session service configuration, event history, context window/summarization), not browser-side chat UI work."}
]}
